The `eval` method contains a nested try-with-resources statement which can be simplified for better readability. Instead of nesting, you can chain resources in the try clause:
```java
try (DoubleBlock valuesBlock = (DoubleBlock) values.eval(page);
     LongBlock percentileBlock = (LongBlock) percentile.eval(page)) {
    return eval(page.getPositionCount(), valuesBlock, percentileBlock);
}
```
